From 4e3d82f69a64cbe6a4dd9a86b348c756313c7b51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominikos Pritis <idominikos@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:59:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: Add Audient iD24 mixer map

For 7.2, which has no Audient mixer map at all.  From 7.3-rc2 upstream
carries the first entry below by itself (commit c53f5bfc3700, "ALSA:
usb-audio: Add mixer map quirk for Audient iD24"), and the 7.3 patch adds
only the other two.

FEATURE_UNIT 12 advertises Volume on 4 of the 6 channels of MIXER_UNIT
60, sits on the monitor mixer branch and is traced through to the
Speaker output terminal, so it is exported as "Speaker Playback Volume"
and userspace takes it for the stream master, attenuating the main pair
asymmetrically below 0 dB.  Rename it to "Monitor Mix Playback Volume",
the name upstream gives it from 7.3-rc2.

MIXER_UNIT 60's descriptor is malformed: bmMixerControls is all-ones
with 11 bytes of trailing junk and iMixer is 255 (lsusb prints "Junk at
end of descriptor").  The generic parser turns that into a fully
programmable 16x6 matrix and creates sixteen 6-channel "ADAT-8 Volume"
controls, named after a channel-name string.  The device ACKs SET_CUR on
them with the UAC2 (ICN << 8 | OCN) addressing, but nothing documents
what the cells mean, and alsactl restore rewrites all 96 of them to
-127 dB on every boot and hot-plug.  Ignore the unit.

FEATURE_UNIT 11 stalls GET_RANGE for its Input Gain control (control
11), so the driver falls back to a 0..1 placeholder range and logs
"11:0: cannot get min/max values for control 11 (id 11)" on every
plug and on every read of the control.  Ignore that control; the Phase
Inverter control on the same unit works and stays.

The map was tested on an iD24 (bcdDevice 1.12) on 7.3-rc1: the card
exposes Monitor Mix Playback Volume, the ADAT-8 controls and the Input
Gain placeholder are gone, alsactl store succeeds, and the min/max
message no longer appears.  On 7.2 it builds against 7.2.8 and adds the
same entries to the same table.
---
 sound/usb/mixer_maps.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c b/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c
index ce27fc8..4649a4b 100644
--- a/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c
+++ b/sound/usb/mixer_maps.c
@@ -505,6 +505,26 @@ static const struct usbmix_connector_map gigabyte_b450_connector_map[] = {
 	{}
 };
 
+/* Audient iD24: FU 12 has Volume on only 4 of the 6 channels of MIXER_UNIT
+ * 60, sits on the monitor mixer branch and is traced to the Speaker
+ * terminal, so userspace adopts it as the stream master and attenuates the
+ * main pair asymmetrically below 0 dB.  Give it a non-standard name, as
+ * upstream does from 7.3-rc2.  MIXER_UNIT 60 itself has a malformed
+ * descriptor (the bmMixerControls bitmap is all-ones with 11 bytes of
+ * trailing junk and iMixer is 255), so the generic parser turns it into a
+ * 16x6 matrix of "ADAT-8 Volume" controls named after a channel string;
+ * alsactl restore rewrites all 96 cells to -127 dB at every boot and
+ * hot-plug.  FU 11 stalls GET_RANGE for Input Gain, which leaves a 0..1
+ * placeholder range and logs "cannot get min/max values" on every read.
+ * Drop both.
+ */
+static const struct usbmix_name_map audient_id24_map[] = {
+	{ 11, NULL, 11 },		/* FU, Input Gain: GET_RANGE stalls */
+	{ 12, "Monitor Mix Playback" },	/* FU, partial coverage */
+	{ 60, NULL },			/* MU, malformed descriptor */
+	{}
+};
+
 /*
  * Control map entries
  */
@@ -598,6 +618,11 @@ static const struct usbmix_ctl_map usbmix_ctl_maps[] = {
 		.id = USB_ID(0x25c4, 0x0003),
 		.map = scms_usb3318_map,
 	},
+	{
+		/* Audient iD24 */
+		.id = USB_ID(0x2708, 0x000d),
+		.map = audient_id24_map,
+	},
 	{
 		/* Bose Companion 5 */
 		.id = USB_ID(0x05a7, 0x1020),
-- 
2.55.0

